{% doc %}
  <title>, meta description, canonical link, robots, theme-color, Open Graph and Twitter
  card tags for the current page. Rendered in the <head> of both layouts, after the
  charset and viewport meta tags.

  Brand: the theme setting "שם המותג באתר" (settings.brand_name, e.g. JOY Mobile) is the
  site name — og:site_name and the title suffix. The store name itself (checkout,
  emails) is not touched.

  Title: "<page> | JOY Mobile אילת" — the page's own title (or the SEO title set in the
  admin) first, then the brand and the city (theme setting store_city), the words people
  search with. Tag filters and page numbers join the page part with " – ". A title that
  already contains the brand gets no suffix. Products get the shorter "<product> | JOY
  אילת" (the brand's first word and the city) and lose the importer suffix the POS import
  writes after " – " ("– יבואן רשמי", "– DCS", "– סאני"), so the city stays inside Google's
  ~60-character title cut; a suffix that states the condition ("– יד שנייה", "– מחודש") or a
  model number ("– דגם 24023") stays, and an SEO title set in the admin is used as written.
  Collections, pages and the rest keep the full suffix. The home page, when the admin sets no home
  page title, gets general.meta.home_title ("JOY Mobile אילת | סלולר, מחשבים
  ואלקטרוניקה ללא מע״מ"). Shopify's English titles of the cart, search and 404 pages
  give way to the Hebrew breadcrumb names.

  Description: never empty. The SEO description from the admin, else
  - product: its description as plain text from the first paragraph on (an opening heading is
    skipped), else general.meta.product_description
    (…_tax_free, with "ללא מע״מ", only for a non-taxable variant — the theme's TAX FREE rule);
  - collection: the opening paragraph of its description, else general.meta.collection_description;
  - article: its excerpt or content; page: the opening paragraph of its body;
  - all categories (/collections): general.meta.collections_description; a blog without an SEO
    description: general.meta.blog_description;
  - anything else, the home page included: general.meta.default_description.
  Generated descriptions are plain text cut at 160 characters (snippets/plain-text).
  Title and description print with escape_once: the `t` filter has already escaped the
  values it fills in (a title with "&"), and must not be escaped twice.

  Canonical: Shopify's canonical_url, without filter, sort or variant parameters.
  Paginated pages stay indexable with a self canonical: canonical_url keeps ?page=N, and
  the parameter is added should it ever be missing.

  Robots: "noindex, follow" on search results and on collection URLs with an active
  storefront filter (filter.* parameters) or a sort_by parameter — near-copies of the
  collection whose links are still worth following. The in-stock filter alone
  (filter.v.availability=1) does NOT count: layout/theme.liquid sends every category visit to
  that URL, so it is the category itself, and a noindex there would drop the category from
  Google (Googlebot renders the page and follows the redirect). Also "noindex, follow": the
  collections listed in the theme setting seo_noindex_collections (default frontpage,
  vendors, types — empty or catch-all pages), any product, collection, page or article whose
  seo.hidden metafield is 1 (Shopify's own "hide from search engines" flag, which also takes it
  out of the sitemap), and the 404 page. Every other page allows large image previews
  (max-image-preview:large). No hreflang: both JOY sites are Hebrew for Israel, and hreflang
  only points to alternate languages or regions.

  Canonical override: a product, collection, page or article with the metafield
  custom.canonical_url (type URL) uses it as its canonical and og:url — for a copy whose
  original lives elsewhere: a pre-merge single-colour product whose colour is now a variant of
  another product, or an Eilat product whose national twin is the page that should rank.

  SEO settings (theme settings › קידום אתרים):
  - seo_collection_title_modifier: words added after a category's name when the admin sets no
    SEO title ("סמארטפונים – מחירים ומשלוח עד הבית | JOY Mobile").
  - seo_product_description_lead: an opening for generated product descriptions, with the
    tokens [title] and [price] ("[title] ב-[price] עם משלוח עד הבית."), followed by the
    description itself and cut at 160 characters, so the two JOY sites' copies of a product
    don't share one snippet.
  A product title with no Hebrew letter ("Samsung Galaxy Z Flip 8") gets the Hebrew noun of
  its product type ("– טלפון סלולרי"), the words Hebrew searches use. SEO descriptions carried
  over from Konimbo ("…? הכנסו>>") are ignored and the generated description is used instead.
  A category without a description gets a generated one with its product count and leading
  brands. A category without an image shares its first product's photo.

  Share image: pages without their own image use the theme setting "תמונת שיתוף"
  (share_image), else assets/social-share.jpg (1200×630, the JOY Mobile lockup on navy).
  og:locale is he_IL.

  @example
  {% render 'meta-tags' %}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign brand_name = settings.brand_name | strip | default: shop.name
  assign store_city = settings.store_city | strip
  assign title_suffix = brand_name
  if store_city != blank
    assign title_suffix = brand_name | append: ' ' | append: store_city
  endif

  # The page part of the title. Shopify's page_title is the shop name where a page has no title of its own.
  assign base_title = page_title | strip
  if base_title == shop.name
    assign base_title = ''
  endif
  case request.page_type
    when 'list-collections'
      assign base_title = 'general.breadcrumbs.all_collections' | t
    when 'cart'
      assign base_title = 'general.breadcrumbs.cart' | t
    when '404'
      assign base_title = 'general.breadcrumbs.not_found' | t
    when 'search'
      assign base_title = 'general.breadcrumbs.search' | t
      if search.terms != blank
        capture search_shown
          render 'search-query', terms: search.terms, format: 'display'
        endcapture
        assign base_title = base_title | append: ': ' | append: search_shown
      endif
    when 'password'
      assign base_title = ''
  endcase

  assign meta_suffix = title_suffix
  if request.page_type == 'product'
    assign meta_suffix = brand_name | split: ' ' | first
    if store_city != blank
      assign meta_suffix = meta_suffix | append: ' ' | append: store_city
    endif
    if product.metafields.global.title_tag.value == blank and base_title contains ' – '
      assign meta_head = base_title | split: ' – ' | first | strip
      assign meta_tail = base_title | remove_first: meta_head | remove_first: ' – ' | strip
      assign meta_tail_start = meta_tail | slice: 0, 3
      unless meta_tail contains 'יד שני' or meta_tail contains 'מחודש' or meta_tail_start == 'דגם' or meta_head == blank
        assign base_title = meta_head
      endunless
    endif
    # A Latin-only title ("Samsung Galaxy Z Flip 8") misses the Hebrew words people search with:
    # the product type's Hebrew noun is added ("Samsung Galaxy Z Flip 8 – טלפון סלולרי").
    if product.metafields.global.title_tag.value == blank and base_title != blank
      capture meta_type_noun
        render 'seo-type-noun', title: base_title, type: product.type
      endcapture
      assign meta_type_noun = meta_type_noun | strip
      if meta_type_noun != blank
        assign base_title = base_title | append: ' – ' | append: meta_type_noun
      endif
    endif
  endif

  # A category without an SEO title of its own: the theme's modifier after its name.
  if request.page_type == 'collection' and current_tags == blank and base_title != blank
    assign meta_collection_modifier = settings.seo_collection_title_modifier | strip
    if meta_collection_modifier != blank and collection.metafields.global.title_tag.value == blank and collection.handle != 'vendors' and collection.handle != 'types'
      assign base_title = base_title | append: ' ' | append: meta_collection_modifier
    endif
  endif

  assign meta_title = base_title
  if current_tags
    assign meta_tag_list = current_tags | join: ', '
    if request.page_type == 'blog'
      # Article tags are collection handles ("televisions"): use the collection's title,
      # else the tag itself (same rule as sections/main-blog and the breadcrumbs).
      assign meta_tag_list = ''
      for tag in current_tags
        assign meta_tag_name = collections[tag].title | default: tag
        unless forloop.first
          assign meta_tag_list = meta_tag_list | append: ', '
        endunless
        assign meta_tag_list = meta_tag_list | append: meta_tag_name
      endfor
    endif
    assign meta_tags_text = 'general.meta.tags' | t: tags: meta_tag_list
    assign meta_title = meta_title | append: ' – ' | append: meta_tags_text
  endif
  if current_page != 1
    assign meta_page_text = 'general.meta.page' | t: page: current_page
    assign meta_title = meta_title | append: ' – ' | append: meta_page_text
  endif

  if request.page_type == 'index' and meta_title == blank
    assign meta_title = 'general.meta.home_title' | t: site: title_suffix
  elsif meta_title == blank
    assign meta_title = title_suffix
  else
    unless meta_title contains brand_name
      assign meta_title = meta_title | append: ' | ' | append: meta_suffix
    endunless
  endif
-%}
{%- liquid
  # An SEO description set in the admin wins. Without one, Shopify's page_description for a product,
  # collection, article or page is its body with the tags stripped, which glues the last word of a
  # paragraph to the first word of the next ("מתקדמתאייפון"), so those are flattened here instead.
  assign explicit_description = ''
  case request.page_type
    when 'product'
      assign explicit_description = product.metafields.global.description_tag.value
    when 'collection'
      assign explicit_description = collection.metafields.global.description_tag.value
    when 'article'
      assign explicit_description = article.metafields.global.description_tag.value
    when 'page'
      assign explicit_description = page.metafields.global.description_tag.value
    when 'index', 'search', 'cart', '404', 'list-collections', 'blog'
      assign explicit_description = page_description
  endcase
  # SEO descriptions imported from Konimbo ("ג׳וי מובייל - חנות סלולר … <product>? הכנסו>>") repeat one
  # store blurb on hundreds of products: the generated description is better.
  if explicit_description contains 'הכנסו>>' or explicit_description contains 'הכנסו&gt;&gt;'
    assign explicit_description = ''
  endif

  # The theme's opening for generated product descriptions ([title], [price]).
  assign meta_product_lead = ''
  if request.page_type == 'product' and explicit_description == blank and settings.seo_product_description_lead != blank
    assign meta_lead_price = product.selected_or_first_available_variant.price | money_without_trailing_zeros | strip_html
    assign meta_product_lead = settings.seo_product_description_lead | strip | replace: '[title]', product.title | replace: '[price]', meta_lead_price
  endif
-%}
{%- capture meta_description -%}
  {%- if explicit_description != blank -%}
    {%- render 'plain-text', html: explicit_description -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- case request.page_type -%}
      {%- when 'product' -%}
        {%- liquid
          # From the first paragraph on: a heading that opens the description is not a sentence.
          assign meta_product_html = product.description
          if meta_product_html contains '<p'
            assign meta_product_head = meta_product_html | split: '<p' | first
            if meta_product_head != blank
              assign meta_product_html = meta_product_html | remove_first: meta_product_head
            endif
          endif
        -%}
        {%- liquid
          if meta_product_lead != blank
            assign meta_product_html = meta_product_lead | escape | append: ' ' | append: meta_product_html
          endif
        -%}
        {%- render 'plain-text', html: meta_product_html, limit: 160 -%}
      {%- when 'collection' -%}
        {%- render 'plain-text', html: collection.description, first_paragraph: true, limit: 160 -%}
      {%- when 'article' -%}
        {%- render 'plain-text', html: article.excerpt_or_content, first_paragraph: true, limit: 160 -%}
      {%- when 'page' -%}
        {%- render 'plain-text', html: page.content, first_paragraph: true, limit: 160 -%}
    {%- endcase -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- liquid
  if meta_description == blank
    case request.page_type
      when 'product'
        assign meta_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
        if meta_variant.taxable == false
          assign meta_description = 'general.meta.product_description_tax_free' | t: title: product.title, site: title_suffix
        else
          assign meta_description = 'general.meta.product_description' | t: title: product.title, site: title_suffix
        endif
      when 'collection'
        # Product count and up to three leading brands (snippets/seo-collection-brands), e.g.
        # "סמארטפונים ב-JOY Mobile: 219 מוצרים של Apple, Samsung ו-Xiaomi ועוד. …".
        capture meta_brand_text
          render 'seo-collection-brands', collection: collection, brand_name: brand_name
        endcapture
        assign meta_brand_text = meta_brand_text | strip
        if collection.all_products_count > 0 and meta_brand_text != blank
          assign meta_description = 'general.meta.collection_description_rich' | t: title: collection.title, site: title_suffix, count: collection.all_products_count, brands: meta_brand_text
        else
          assign meta_description = 'general.meta.collection_description' | t: title: collection.title, site: title_suffix
        endif
      when 'list-collections'
        assign meta_description = 'general.meta.collections_description' | t: brand: brand_name
      when 'blog'
        assign meta_description = 'general.meta.blog_description' | t: title: blog.title, brand: brand_name
      else
        assign meta_description = 'general.meta.default_description' | t: brand: brand_name
    endcase
  endif

  # Search results and filtered or sorted collection URLs: out of the index, links still followed.
  # The in-stock filter on its own (filter.v.availability=1) is the category itself: layout/theme.liquid
  # sends every category visit there, Googlebot included, so it must stay indexable.
  assign robots_noindex = false
  if request.page_type == 'search' or request.page_type == '404'
    assign robots_noindex = true
  elsif request.page_type == 'collection'
    if collection.sort_by != blank
      assign robots_noindex = true
    endif
    for filter in collection.filters
      if filter.param_name == 'filter.v.availability'
        for meta_active in filter.active_values
          if meta_active.value != '1'
            assign robots_noindex = true
          endif
        endfor
        continue
      endif
      if filter.active_values.size > 0 or filter.min_value.value != blank or filter.max_value.value != blank
        assign robots_noindex = true
        break
      endif
    endfor
    # Empty or catch-all categories named in the theme settings (frontpage, vendors, types, …).
    assign meta_noindex_handles = settings.seo_noindex_collections | default: 'frontpage, vendors, types' | split: ','
    for meta_noindex_handle in meta_noindex_handles
      assign meta_noindex_handle = meta_noindex_handle | strip
      if meta_noindex_handle != blank and collection.handle == meta_noindex_handle
        assign robots_noindex = true
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  # Shopify's "hide from search engines" flag (metafield seo.hidden = 1) and the canonical override.
  assign meta_resource = nil
  case request.page_type
    when 'product'
      assign meta_resource = product
    when 'collection'
      assign meta_resource = collection
    when 'page'
      assign meta_resource = page
    when 'article'
      assign meta_resource = article
  endcase
  assign meta_canonical_override = ''
  if meta_resource != nil
    assign meta_hidden = meta_resource.metafields.seo.hidden.value | append: ''
    if meta_hidden == '1'
      assign robots_noindex = true
    endif
    assign meta_canonical_override = meta_resource.metafields.custom.canonical_url.value | append: '' | strip
  endif

  # Paginated pages keep their own canonical (…?page=2).
  assign canonical = canonical_url
  if current_page > 1
    assign canonical_page = 'page=' | append: current_page
    unless canonical contains canonical_page
      if canonical contains '?'
        assign canonical = canonical | append: '&' | append: canonical_page
      else
        assign canonical = canonical | append: '?' | append: canonical_page
      endif
    endunless
  endif

  # custom.canonical_url: the original of a copy (a pre-merge product, a twin on the other JOY site).
  if current_page == 1 and meta_canonical_override contains 'https://'
    assign canonical = meta_canonical_override
  endif

  assign og_type = 'website'
  assign og_title = base_title | default: meta_title
  assign og_image = page_image | default: settings.share_image
  # A category without its own image shares its first product's photo rather than the logo card.
  if request.page_type == 'collection' and collection.image == blank and collection.products.first.featured_media != blank
    assign og_image = collection.products.first.featured_media.preview_image
  endif
  case request.page_type
    when 'index'
      assign og_title = meta_title
    when 'product'
      assign og_type = 'product'
      # Same head as <title> (no " – יבואן רשמי" tail), so a shared link previews the product name.
      assign og_title = base_title | default: product.title
    when 'article'
      assign og_type = 'article'
      assign og_title = article.title
    when 'password'
      assign og_title = brand_name
  endcase
-%}
<title>{{ meta_title | escape_once }}</title>
<meta name="description" content="{{ meta_description | escape_once }}">
{%- unless request.page_type == '404' %}
<link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical }}">
{%- endunless %}
{%- if robots_noindex %}
<meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">
{%- else %}
<meta name="robots" content="max-image-preview:large">
{%- endif %}
<meta name="theme-color" content="{{ settings.color_header_bg }}">
<meta property="og:site_name" content="{{ brand_name | escape }}">
<meta property="og:url" content="{{ canonical }}">
<meta property="og:title" content="{{ og_title | escape_once }}">
<meta property="og:type" content="{{ og_type }}">
<meta property="og:description" content="{{ meta_description | escape_once }}">
<meta property="og:locale" content="he_IL">
{%- if og_image != blank %}
  {%- assign og_image_url = og_image | image_url: width: 1200 -%}
<meta property="og:image" content="https:{{ og_image_url | remove_first: 'https:' }}">
<meta property="og:image:secure_url" content="https:{{ og_image_url | remove_first: 'https:' }}">
<meta property="og:image:width" content="{{ og_image.width | at_most: 1200 }}">
<meta property="og:image:height" content="{{ og_image.height | times: 1.0 | divided_by: og_image.width | times: 1200 | at_most: og_image.height | round }}">
<meta property="og:image:alt" content="{{ og_image.alt | default: og_title | escape_once }}">
{%- else %}
  {%- assign share_image_url = 'social-share.jpg' | asset_url | remove_first: 'https:' | prepend: 'https:' -%}
<meta property="og:image" content="{{ share_image_url }}">
<meta property="og:image:secure_url" content="{{ share_image_url }}">
<meta property="og:image:type" content="image/jpeg">
<meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">
<meta property="og:image:height" content="630">
<meta property="og:image:alt" content="{{ brand_name | escape }}">
{%- endif %}
{%- if request.page_type == 'product' %}
<meta property="product:price:amount" content="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.price | divided_by: 100.0 }}">
<meta property="product:price:currency" content="{{ cart.currency.iso_code | default: shop.currency }}">
<meta property="product:availability" content="{% if product.available %}in stock{% else %}out of stock{% endif %}">
{%- endif %}
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
<meta name="twitter:title" content="{{ og_title | escape_once }}">
<meta name="twitter:description" content="{{ meta_description | escape_once }}">
